(The word "as" turns a value into another type: "the pi as a number".)

Print "=== Number and Float Conversions ===".

(A float becomes a number by dropping everything after the point)
A float called pi is 3.14159.
A number called 'pi truncated' is the pi as a number.
Print "3.14159 as number: ".
Print the 'pi truncated'.

A number called quantity is 42.
A float called 'quantity as a float' is the quantity as a float.
Print "42 as float: ".
Print the 'quantity as a float'.

(Adding a half before truncating rounds to the nearest whole number; the
 braces make the sum happen before the cast)
A float called measurement is 3.7.
A number called rounded is {the measurement add 0.5} as a number.
Print "3.7 rounded: ".
Print the rounded.

Print "".
Print "=== Number and Text Conversions ===".

A number called age is 25.
Print "Age: ".
Print the age as text.

Print "".
Print "=== Boolean and Number Conversions ===".

A boolean called 'switched on' is true.
A number called 'on as a number' is the 'switched on' as a number.
Print "true as number: ".
Print the 'on as a number'.

A boolean called 'switched off' is false.
A number called 'off as a number' is the 'switched off' as a number.
Print "false as number: ".
Print the 'off as a number'.

Print "".
Print "=== Inline Casting ===".

Print "Direct cast 3.99 as number: ".
Print 3.99 as a number.

Print "".
Print "=== Done ===".
